ration-150"><div class="relative"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 py-6 sm:py-7"><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="m-0 transition-colors duration-150 text-[18px] sm:text-[21px] leading-[1.3]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.9)">How is this different from other tools?</h3></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-[26px] leading-none transition-colors duration-150" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:300;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5)">+</span></div><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-panel-_R_qhanrlb_" class="absolute inset-0 w-full cursor-pointer"><span class="sr-only">How is this different from other tools?</span></button></div><div id="accordion-panel-_R_qhanrlb_" class="grid" style="grid-template-rows:0fr;visibility:hidden;transition:grid-template-rows 260ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), visibility 0s 260ms"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-7"><p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] max-w-[58ch]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6)">Most alternatives are point solutions. One does search, another does browsers, another does scraping. TinyFish is the only platform that puts TinySearch, TinyFetch, TinyBrowser, and TinyAgent behind one API key and one Wallet.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="[&amp;&gt;div]:px-6" style="border-top:1px solid rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08)"><div class=" transition-colors duration-150"><div class="relative"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 py-6 sm:py-7"><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="m-0 transition-colors duration-150 text-[18px] sm:text-[21px] leading-[1.3]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.9)">Why would I use this instead of my LLM&#x27;s built-in web search?</h3></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-[26px] leading-none transition-colors duration-150" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:300;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5)">+</span></div><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-panel-_R_1ahanrlb_" class="absolute inset-0 w-full cursor-pointer"><span class="sr-only">Why would I use this instead of my LLM&#x27;s built-in web search?</span></button></div><div id="accordion-panel-_R_1ahanrlb_" class="grid" style="grid-template-rows:0fr;visibility:hidden;transition:grid-template-rows 260ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), visibility 0s 260ms"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-7"><p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] max-w-[58ch]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6)">Reliability and structure. Our search hits Google&#x27;s actual live index through a real browser, not a secondary index or cached results. You get typed JSON objects back, not markdown blobs your model has to parse.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="[&amp;&gt;div]:px-6" style="border-top:1px solid rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08)"><div class=" transition-colors duration-150"><div class="relative"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 py-6 sm:py-7"><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="m-0 transition-colors duration-150 text-[18px] sm:text-[21px] leading-[1.3]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.9)">How accurate is TinyAgent?</h3></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-[26px] leading-none transition-colors duration-150" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:300;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5)">+</span></div><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-panel-_R_1qhanrlb_" class="absolute inset-0 w-full cursor-pointer"><span class="sr-only">How accurate is TinyAgent?</span></button></div><div id="accordion-panel-_R_1qhanrlb_" class="grid" style="grid-template-rows:0fr;visibility:hidden;transition:grid-template-rows 260ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), visibility 0s 260ms"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-7"><p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] max-w-[58ch]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6)">89.9% overall on Mind2Web, the industry-standard benchmark for web agents. 81.9% on hard tasks, where Operator scores 43.2% and Claude scores 32.4%. All 300 runs are open-sourced and independently verifiable.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="[&amp;&gt;div]:px-6" style="border-top:1px solid rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08)"><div class=" transition-colors duration-150"><div class="relative"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 py-6 sm:py-7"><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="m-0 transition-colors duration-150 text-[18px] sm:text-[21px] leading-[1.3]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.9)">Can agents authenticate into websites?</h3></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-[26px] leading-none transition-colors duration-150" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);font-weight:300;color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5)">+</span></div><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-panel-_R_2ahanrlb_" class="absolute inset-0 w-full cursor-pointer"><span class="sr-only">Can agents authenticate into websites?</span></button></div><div id="accordion-panel-_R_2ahanrlb_" class="grid" style="grid-template-rows:0fr;visibility:hidden;transition:grid-template-rows 260ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), visibility 0s 260ms"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-7"><p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] max-w-[58ch]" style="font-family:var(--font-inter);color:rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6)">Yes. TinyVault lets agents log into portals, navigate authenticated dashboards, and extract from gated content without exposing credentials to the LLM.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div aria-hidden="true" class="h-0"></div><section id="home-closing" class="relative w-full overflow-hidden" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08)"><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 max-sm:opacity-50" style="mask-image:radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 48% 